A||||2||eastex87gt||Lights coming on all over the place||||9||
Z||000000||eastex87gt||07-05-2001||08:03 PM||||I was driving home today in my 87 gt and my check engine, volt, and oil light all came on at the same time.  All the gauges showed to be ok but after 20 seconds the engine died.  It cranked right back up and I made it home but it did it again as i was pulling in the driveway.  This time it didn't die but the lights came on.  The gauges all had normal read outs.  Please help!!!||||reg||9
Z||000001||FieroJoe||07-05-2001||10:25 PM||||Well, the first place to start is to do a check over of your engine, and make sure that there arent any fried wires or obvious problems like that.  Next, the engine dying part could be an overheated ignition module.  This is common with V6's.  When it first died, the module cooled down until you could start it again and make it back home, until it got hot and shut down again.<P>That's just one thing that could be wrong.  About the gauges going whacky, all I can assume is that possibly, if it is indeed a overheated ignition module, that it sent some sort of electrical interference out into the car and made that happen.<P>I hope this gets you started, like I said, the first best thing is to do a general check of the engine, and fuses too while you're at it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||eastex87gt||07-05-2001||11:45 PM||||Thanks for your help.  I'll check it out in the morning.||||reg||1
